A_300 - If you're feeling a little off and you're male, you can try something similar to what I tried: I poured a little mouthwash on my foreskin, and after some initial discomfort (probably due to the fluoride and other active ingredients present, which aren't meant for that part of the body) it turned into a rather pleasant sensation. If you'd rather try a similar sensation with fewer harsh chemicals, you can place a mint there instead of mouthwash: the menthol gives a similar cooling sensation, without the alcohol and fluoride of mouthwash (though menthol itself can still cause some irritation in some people). Either way, if you notice redness or lasting discomfort, stop and don't repeat it.